+-- Strings GlueStrings.lua has for the ten stock classes and cannot have for this one.
+-- They live here rather than in a GlueStrings.lua override because that file is 77 KB of
+-- locale data in enUS/patch-enUS-3.MPQ and forking it to add four strings would mean
+-- re-forking it after every locale change. GlueXML.toc loads GlueStrings.lua first and
+-- CharacterCreate.xml much later, so a real GlueStrings entry still wins if one ever ships.
+--
+-- Only the male form is defined: GetFlavorText() (below) falls back to the other suffix
+-- when its first lookup is nil, so CLASS_FELSWORN covers both sexes the way
+-- CLASS_DEATHKNIGHT and CLASS_DEATHKNIGHT_FEMALE would if they were not identical.
+if ( not CLASS_FELSWORN ) then
